x86_64-linux  three recorded differences and no fourth. The C1/D1 forms of the in-class constructors and destructors beside the C2/D2 - the COMDAT difference implicit-move.nonames records. The inline placement pair declared for the oracle's sake, `_ZnwmPv` and `_ZdlPvS_`, which cxx1 emits as weak definitions where clang elides an inline function nothing calls. And clang's `_Unwind_Resume` with the personality reference: for `new Plain(7)` it keeps a cleanup that frees the storage should the constructor throw, which cxx1 does not build for a new-expression - conditional-class.nonames records the same shape. The allocation names themselves agree: `_Znwm`, `_ZdlPv`, `_ZN6PoolednwEm`, `_ZN6PooleddlEPv`.
x86_64-windows  the placement pair once more, `??2@YAPEAX_KPEAX@Z` and `??3@YAXPEAX0@Z`, emitted where cl elides them; every other name agrees, `??2Pooled@@SAPEAX_K@Z` and `??3Pooled@@SAXPEAX@Z` among them.
arm64-darwin  the same three: `__Unwind_Resume`, `__ZnwmPv`, `__ZdlPvS_`.
